== 5. the reply path, clock by clock
  SETUP data, answered ACK by T2 (clocks from the first SE0 clock of the host's EOP; 40 clocks = 1 bit):
      12  T0 raises IDLE (end of packet seen)
      40  T0 end-of-packet strobe
      46  T2 reply chosen (CRC checked)
      80  host EOP: SE0 to J (turnaround reference)
     138  device drives J
     186  device's first K (SOP)
  IN token, answered with data from the FIFO by T1 (clocks from the first SE0 clock of the host's EOP; 40 clocks = 1 bit):
      16  T0 raises IDLE (end of packet seen)
      44  T0 end-of-packet strobe
      65  T1 reply chosen (token and RDY checked)
      80  host EOP: SE0 to J (turnaround reference)
     141  device drives J
     189  device's first K (SOP)
